// result_end
\caption(The ordinate is explicitly the transformed discrepancy, not a logarithmic axis with an artificial error floor. Larger is better. The grey N-1 line describes the exact tail envelope; coloured points compare doubles with the standard library. Zero discrepancies are omitted and counted.)
\alttext(The ln(pi) accuracy generally grows with the attempted shift count and then approaches double precision. The ln(3) accuracy is flat after its first two factors. The exact tail-envelope accuracy increases linearly as N minus one.)

> Domain-wide numerical controls

The sweep below includes both domain endpoints and 255 interior points for each
mode. Each prefix is obtained from the core API. We compare the largest
logarithm absolute discrepancy and exponential relative discrepancy with the
derived envelope, allowing 1e-14 for accumulated double and reference rounding.
That allowance is a numerical test tolerance, separate from the exact bound.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const auto domain=dm::algorithms::bkm_domain();
  std::print("| N | maximum ln absolute discrepancy | maximum exp relative discrepancy | exact envelope |\n"
             "| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for (int n:{1,2,4,8,16,32,48,53}) {
    double ln_error=0,exp_error=0;
    for (int i=0;i<=256;++i) {
      const double u=i/256.;
      const double v=1+u*(domain.max_argument-1),y=u*domain.max_exponent;
      ln_error=std::max(ln_error,std::abs(dm::algorithms::bkm_ln_trace(v,n).value-std::log(v)));
      exp_error=std::max(exp_error,std::abs(dm::algorithms::bkm_exp_trace(y,n).value/std::exp(y)-1));
    }
    const double envelope=std::ldexp(1.,1-n);
    if (ln_error>envelope+1e-14 || exp_error>envelope+1e-14) return 1;
    std::print("| {} | {:.3e} | {:.3e} | {:.3e} |\n",n,ln_error,exp_error,envelope);
  }
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| N | maximum ln absolute discrepancy | maximum exp relative discrepancy | exact envelope |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 1 | 8.689e-01 | 5.806e-01 | 1.000e+00 |
| 2 | 4.634e-01 | 3.709e-01 | 5.000e-01 |
| 4 | 1.225e-01 | 1.153e-01 | 1.250e-01 |
| 8 | 7.802e-03 | 7.772e-03 | 7.812e-03 |
| 16 | 3.052e-05 | 3.052e-05 | 3.052e-05 |
